Requirements: 6   with obligations: 6

[task-01] The judgement-instability harness in `src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py`
    runs a review several times, and once over a perturbed input, and reports how far
    its judgements move.
    -> runs-review-several-times  [functional/explicit]
       Run a review several times.
    -> perturbed-input-run  [functional/explicit]
       Run the review once over a perturbed input.
    -> judgement-movement-reporting  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Report how far the judgements move across repeated reviews and the perturbed-
       input review.

[task-02] When the harness builds its own model client (no client factory supplied),
    that client must be configured exactly as `RunConfig.build_client()` would configure
    it for the same run configuration, including the embedding model, per-stage models
    and per-stage reasoning settings. The client the harness uses to watch a run must
    accept every argument `ModelClient.complete` accepts and pass each one through
    unchanged, so that a parameter added to `ModelClient` later reaches the pipeline
    without any edit to the harness.
    -> harness-client-matches-runconfig-build-client  [compatibility/explicit]
       When the harness builds its own model client without a supplied client factory,
       it configures that client exactly as `RunConfig.build_client()` would configure
       it for the same run configuration.
    -> watch-client-complete-signature  [compatibility/explicit]
       The client the harness uses to watch a run accepts every argument that
       `ModelClient.complete` accepts.
    -> pass-complete-args-through-unchanged  [functional/explicit]
       The harness's watch client accepts every argument that ModelClient.complete
       accepts and passes each one through unchanged.

[task-03] The perturbation result must state a sensitivity for each judgement axis
    separately: obligation and open-question presence, evidence class, and defect
    verdict. Each axis's sensitivity is the number of judgements on that axis that
    moved, divided by the number of judgements on that axis that were watched, so every
    reported sensitivity lies between 0 and 1. For the defect-verdict axis, the watched
    judgements are the (defect, test) verdicts present in both the baseline and the
    perturbed run. An axis with nothing watched reports no sensitivity, not zero. No
    single sensitivity blended across axes is reported.
    -> separate-axis-sensitivities  [functional/explicit]
       State a sensitivity for each judgement axis separately: obligation and open-
       question presence, evidence class, and defect verdict.
    -> axis-sensitivity-ratio  [functional/explicit]
       Each axis's sensitivity is computed as the number of judgements on that axis that
       moved divided by the number of judgements on that axis that were watched.
    -> sensitivity-bounded-0-to-1  [invariant/explicit]
       Every reported sensitivity lies between 0 and 1.
    -> defect-verdict-watched-judgements  [invariant/explicit]
       For the defect-verdict axis, watch only the (defect, test) verdicts that are
       present in both the baseline run and the perturbed run.
    -> no-watched-axis-no-sensitivity  [invariant/explicit]
       An axis with nothing watched reports no sensitivity, not zero.

[task-04] A regression test is part of the deliverable: one that runs the harness
    through its default client construction over a small recorded case and fails if the
    pipeline's client gains a parameter the harness does not pass on.
    -> regression-test-part-of-deliverable  [test_demand/explicit]
       A regression test is part of the deliverable.
    -> default-client-construction-small-recorded-case  [test_demand/explicit]
       A regression test runs the harness through its default client construction over a
       small recorded case.
    -> client-parameter-forwarding-regression-test  [test_demand/explicit]
       A regression test fails if the pipeline's client gains a parameter the harness
       does not pass on.

[exclusion-01] No change to any prompt or response schema.
    -> prompt-response-schema-unchanged  [docs_config/explicit]
       No change to any prompt or response schema.

[exclusion-02] No change to how the pipeline itself builds or calls its client.
    -> pipeline-client-build-and-call-unchanged  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter how the pipeline itself builds or calls its client.

